From d845791bef78590da94e50d6c20a187eb4cc95e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haogao Gu <koohoko@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:18:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gui: requests without a session ID can fold in Routing

Koohoko reported that the No session ID heading could not fold while
all surrounding session headings could. groupedRows rendered the empty
key as a div and skipped its click handler, arrow and aria-expanded.
Routing classifier calls can fill this group on a busy day.

Make the heading a button and use the existing fold state for its empty
key. Click and Enter fold or expand it, and a live update that moves the
group to the top keeps both the heading element and its fold. The label,
identity tooltip and metric gating retain their previous meaning.

Update the three div-only test selectors and the test README. The new
case covers Chromium/WebKit, en/zh/zh-TW/ja/de, and widths 1100/420. It
uses wheel input for the outer view and nested request list, because
the app deliberately reverses unsolicited automatic scrolling.

Verification on base 674b6ca2881f1289c4ccdec158762978a463320c:
- Final routing-sessions file: 58/58 pass. Its 20 new cases run against
  the unchanged production code: 0 pass, 20 fail, all at aria-expanded
  (null instead of true).
- Initial wider GUI run, 134 files: fixed 1602/1604, base 1600/1600.
  Fixed-only WebKit failures: group-member-weight en 420, 1271 vs 1270
  (same failure class as yetone/magpie#2387); routing-kind zh, one kind
  story after selecting an untagged request, expected zero. Neither
  enables session grouping. Both files subsequently passed 8/8 separate
  runs on each tree. The initial failures remain unexplained; this is
  not an all-green wider run. No assertions in those files changed.
- Go 1.26.8: go test -tags nogui -timeout 45m ./... passes (66 packages
  with tests, 18 without). Temporary HOME, existing Go caches pinned.
- Darwin, Linux (nogui), Windows: vet and build all pass. The first
  attempt lacked cached x/net v0.56.0; after downloading the version
  pinned in go.mod, all checks above completed. Existing Darwin CGImage
  enum-conversion warning remains.
- node --check and git diff --check pass. No Go files changed.
- Synthetic before/after frontend screenshots: six classifier rows
  stay visible before, zero rows after clicking every group heading.

Not run: native Wails window, Linux/Windows devices, complete GUI suite.
The installed app and live gateway were not replaced or restarted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
